      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding some notes here: I'm assuming VRC is using some sort of stateful connection (via websockets?) to pass packets between the client and the server at runtime, but the handling of how these connections can terminate and re-establish needs a look at.\nOne great example is when the send connection is dead but the receive connection hasn't totally died. This leads to the infrequent but very annoying situation where you continue to see everyone else reacting to your frozen, lifeless form for thirty seconds to a minute before the game kicks you out.\nThis is not that easy a situation to solve, but in any competent API (I am personally a gRPC person, but this is usually all HTTP2 under the hood) it's not usually hard to detect when a connection is down and re-establish it.\nVRC should look into when the send/receive goes down and more aggressively handle the situation. Informing the user of the connection being down immediately would be much better than the current buggy system.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
