  "details": "VRChat Version: 2022.1.1p2 (live)\nDescription of the bug:\nThe 'connection timed out' error message and forced reconnect shows up after (potentially only after) connection has be restored.\nThis is evident because there will be several seconds where you can communicate, both hearing and being heard by other players in the instance, before it kicks you out for connection problems. \nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?): \nThis is easiest to test if you have two people talking/moving so you can more easily see when somebody has regained connection.\nStep 1: Connect to a VRChat instance.\nStep 2: Get disconnected temporarily for whatever reason (Simplest way I know how to do this is changing networks and then changing back)\nStep 3: Re-establish your working connection\nStep 4: You should have several seconds of working connection and then get an error message and be forced to reload the instance.\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\nVideo of this happening to me, Connection drops at 0:09, and is clearly regained around 0:30 when you can hear Vowgan start talking and see people resume moving. Then, at 0:40 I get the connection timed out error (which unfortunately does not enter frame):\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1Iw76d74EdSen_cDptydiosUNwZPL-NpS/view?usp=sharing",
